_:nc96241b26f3e46cabb7903a4a2cdaa0cxb0 <http://schema.org/articleBody> "<p>The US is taking more action to stop US chip sales to Huawei by revoking licenses from Intel and Qualcomm to export certain processors to the Chinese tech company.&nbsp;</p><p>The White House has imposed sanctions on Huawei since 2019, forcing US companies to apply for a license to continue such sales.&nbsp;But on Tuesday, the Commerce Department took the additional action of stripping away pre-existing licenses for Qualcomm and Intel. </p><p>This comes weeks after some Republican lawmakers were <a href=\"https://www.cnbc.com/2024/04/15/us-lawmakers-angry-after-huawei-unveils-laptop-with-new-intel-ai-chip.html\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"(Opens in a new tab)\">angered</a> to learn that Huawei launched a Windows laptop using Intel&rsquo;s latest Core Ultra processors.&nbsp;</p><p>In Intel&rsquo;s case, the company secured export licenses from the Trump administration to sell consumer-focused laptops chips to Huawei. <a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/technology/intel-survived-bid-halt-millions-sales-chinas-huawei-sources-say-2024-03-12/\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"(Opens in a new tab)\">According</a> to Reuters, the licenses were supposed to expire later this year and were not expected to be renewed. Meanwhile, Qualcomm obtained a license to sell older 4G-related chips to the Chinese company.&nbsp;</p><img src=\"data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20768%20432'%3E%3Crect%20fill='%23f7f7f7'%20/%3E%3C/svg%3E\" class=\"\" data-image-loader=\"https://i.pcmag.com/imagery/articles/02kPeOFaaIdmU9lgCpkhkrI-2.jpg\" data-lazy-sized alt=\"Huawei Mate X Pro\" data-image-path=\"articles/02kPeOFaaIdmU9lgCpkhkrI-2.jpg\">\n<div style=\"line-height:1.25 !important\" class=\"-mt-4 mb-8\">\n    <small>Huawei Mate X Pro (Credit: CFOTO/Future Publishing via Getty Images)</small>\n</div>\n<p>But on Tuesday, US Rep. Michael McCaul (R-Texas) said the Commerce Department had revoked the licenses in an effort to further block processor sales to Huawei. Intel and Qualcomm \"are two companies we&rsquo;ve always worried about being a little too close to China,&rdquo; McCaul <a href=\"https://www.msn.com/en-us/money/other/us-revokes-intel-qualcomm-licenses-to-sell-chips-to-huawei/ar-BB1lZqJO\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"(Opens in a new tab)\">told</a> Bloomberg.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>The Commerce Department hasn&rsquo;t specified which permits were canceled. But in an SEC <a href=\"https://www.intc.com/filings-reports/all-sec-filings/content/0000050863-24-000086/0000050863-24-000086.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"(Opens in a new tab)\">filing</a> on Wednesday, Intel confirmed that the US agency had pulled &ldquo;certain licenses for exports of consumer-related items to a customer in China, effective immediately.&rdquo;&nbsp;</p><div class=\"py-4\" data-parent-group=\"related-stories\">\n    <div class=\"mx-0 border border-b border-l-0 border-r-0 border-t border-gray-300 py-4 md:ml-8 md:mr-24\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-stretch-ultra-condensed mb-2 text-lg font-semibold uppercase\">Recommended by Our Editors</h3>\n        <div class=\"flex flex-wrap\">\n                            <div class=\"my-4 inline-flex w-full md:my-2\">\n                    \n                    <a class=\"mr-4 inline min-w-24 max-w-24 no-underline md:min-w-28 md:max-w-28\" data-module=\"related-recirc\" data-item=\"related-recirc-list\" data-element=\"related-recirc-image\" data-position=\"1\" data-title=\"Huawei logo\" href=\"/news/effort-to-rip-and-replace-huawei-zte-tech-in-us-backfires-due-to-funding\" x-track-ga-click>\n                                            <div class=\"relative aspect-video overflow-hidden\">\n                            <img class=\"absolute inset-1/2 h-auto w-auto translate-center\" data-image-loader=\"https://i.pcmag.com/imagery/articles/03ZUxIpjapgUORQr2rWDhek-1.fit_lpad.size_400x225.v1714680889.jpg\" data-lazy-sized src=\"data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20400%20225'%3E%3Crect%20fill='%23f7f7f7'%20/%3E%3C/svg%3E\" alt=\"Huawei logo\">\n                        </div>\n                                        </a>\n                    <div class=\"flex w-auto flex-col justify-center md:mr-20\">\n                        \n                        <a class=\"inline-block align-middle leading-tight no-underline\" data-module=\"related-recirc\" data-item=\"related-recirc-list\" data-element=\"related-recirc-link\" data-position=\"1\" href=\"/news/effort-to-rip-and-replace-huawei-zte-tech-in-us-backfires-due-to-funding\" x-track-ga-click>Effort to 'Rip and Replace' Huawei, ZTE Tech in US Backfires Due to Funding Woes</a>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n                            <div class=\"my-4 inline-flex w-full md:my-2\">\n                    \n                    <a class=\"mr-4 inline min-w-24 max-w-24 no-underline md:min-w-28 md:max-w-28\" data-module=\"related-recirc\" data-item=\"related-recirc-list\" data-element=\"related-recirc-image\" data-position=\"2\" data-title=\"Mate 60 phone\" href=\"/news/what-us-sanctions-huawei-mate-60-pro-launches-with-korean-memory-chip\" x-track-ga-click>\n                                            <div class=\"relative aspect-video overflow-hidden\">\n                            <img class=\"absolute inset-1/2 h-auto w-auto translate-center\" data-image-loader=\"https://i.pcmag.com/imagery/articles/04LSNMZXIVVf3vLRhuegCuX-1.fit_lpad.size_400x225.v1694095351.jpg\" data-lazy-sized src=\"data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20400%20225'%3E%3Crect%20fill='%23f7f7f7'%20/%3E%3C/svg%3E\" alt=\"Mate 60 phone\">\n                        </div>\n                                        </a>\n                    <div class=\"flex w-auto flex-col justify-center md:mr-20\">\n                        \n                        <a class=\"inline-block align-middle leading-tight no-underline\" data-module=\"related-recirc\" data-item=\"related-recirc-list\" data-element=\"related-recirc-link\" data-position=\"2\" href=\"/news/what-us-sanctions-huawei-mate-60-pro-launches-with-korean-memory-chip\" x-track-ga-click>What US Sanctions? Huawei Mate 60 Pro Launches With Korean Memory Chip</a>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n                            <div class=\"my-4 inline-flex w-full md:my-2\">\n                    \n                    <a class=\"mr-4 inline min-w-24 max-w-24 no-underline md:min-w-28 md:max-w-28\" data-module=\"related-recirc\" data-item=\"related-recirc-list\" data-element=\"related-recirc-image\" data-position=\"3\" data-title=\"Huawei\" href=\"/news/huawei-tries-to-sidestep-us-sanctions-using-secret-chip-manufacturing-plants\" x-track-ga-click>\n                                            <div class=\"relative aspect-video overflow-hidden\">\n                            <img class=\"absolute inset-1/2 h-auto w-auto translate-center\" data-image-loader=\"https://i.pcmag.com/imagery/articles/04Wld4mPGHPSA1kLEg1mMk8-1.fit_lpad.size_400x225.v1692786167.jpg\" data-lazy-sized src=\"data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20400%20225'%3E%3Crect%20fill='%23f7f7f7'%20/%3E%3C/svg%3E\" alt=\"Huawei\">\n                        </div>\n                                        </a>\n                    <div class=\"flex w-auto flex-col justify-center md:mr-20\">\n                        \n                        <a class=\"inline-block align-middle leading-tight no-underline\" data-module=\"related-recirc\" data-item=\"related-recirc-list\" data-element=\"related-recirc-link\" data-position=\"3\" href=\"/news/huawei-tries-to-sidestep-us-sanctions-using-secret-chip-manufacturing-plants\" x-track-ga-click>Huawei Tries to Sidestep US Sanctions Using Secret Chip-Manufacturing Plants</a>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n                    </div>\n    </div>\n</div>\n<p>&ldquo;As a result, the company expects revenue for the second quarter of 2024 to remain in the original range of $12.5 billion to $13.5 billion, but below the midpoint,&rdquo; Intel added.&nbsp;</p><p>Huawei didn&rsquo;t immediately respond to a request for comment. It could affect laptop and smartphone sales, although Huawei has been finding ways to <a href=\"https://qz.com/china-huawei-us-tech-advanced-chip-1851319496\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"(Opens in a new tab)\">bypass</a> US sanctions by developing its own processors and software for consumer products.</p>" <https://www.pcmag.com/news/us-pulls-licenses-that-intel-qualcomm-used-to-sell-chips-to-huawei>   .
