_:n0f376d0f97df4faaa79d38b91c69ddf0xb0 <http://schema.org/description> "THE BOSS PEN IS A STATEMENT PIECE. THIS LUXURY PEN HAS THE STRENGTH\nOF RHODIUM COMBINED WITH HAND CAST 22K GOLD ACCENTS AND TAKES THE WARM\nCHARISMA OF TIMBER TO CREATE AN INSPIRED WRITING EXPERIENCE. IT IS A\nPEN OF DISTINCTION. $1 FROM THE SALE OF THIS PEN GOES\nTOWARDS PLANTING TREES TO REFOREST AUSTRALIA WITH REFOREST NOW.\n[https://www.reforestnow.org.au/about] PLUS AT CHECKOUT YOU\nCAN PLANT ONE TREE AND RECEIVE A TREE PLANTING CERTIFICATE.\n\n \t* Available as a fountain pen or rollerball pen.\n \t* Hand cast 22k gold accents.\n \t* Gorgeous rhodium plating (hard wearing, resistant to corrosion,\nwill not oxidize).\n \t* Non post-able end cap.\n \t* 130 mm pen body  is designed to show off the timber.\n \t* Weight is approximately 26 grams (cap off), 48 grams with cap on.\n \t* Pen body is 13 mm wide.\n \t* Handcrafted by Brisbane wood artisans using precision and flair.\n \t* Meticulous 10 step sanding & polishing process.\n \t* Individually hand lacquered with 14 layers of finish polished to a\nhigh sheen.\n \t* The Boss pen comes to you in an eco pen box. It also looks\nstunning presented in a black gift pen box or engrave-able  timber\nbox.\n\nFOUNTAIN PEN\n\n \t* Quality Bock #5 nib in medium supplied. A fine or broad nib\nare available on request.\n \t* Approx 0.5 mm of writing width.\n \t* Jowo nib upgrades available here.\n[https://www.veridianpenstudio.com.au/product/jowo-fountain-pen-nib]\n \t* Easily replaceable international standard ink cartridges (one\nsupplied).\n \t* Environmentally friendly piston converter to refill from bottled\nink (supplied).\n \t* Purchase a bottle of fountain pen ink here.\n[https://www.veridianpenstudio.com.au/shop/all-inks]\n\nROLLERBALL PEN\n\n \t* Comfortable rhodium plated grip for easy writing.\n \t* Loaded with a premium Schmidt refill – black (fine) for\nunrivalled writing (medium or blue available on request).\n\nCOTTONWOOD TIMBER\n\nCottonwood is an introduced species to Australia, it is a popular and\ncommon coastal plant in Eastern and Northern Australia. It is also\nknown as beach hibiscus. The flowers are bright yellow with a deep red\ncentre upon opening. The sapwood is pale and the heartwood is very\ndark grey to black, the grain is frequently fine. The timber is used\nin seacraft construction, furniture and wood\n[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wood_carving]carvings. Its tough bark\ncan be made into durable rope and traditionally used for sealing\ncracks in boats.\n\nPERSONALISATION: We personalise timber pens and wooden pen boxes. In\nthe text box provided:\n\n \t* PEN LASER ENGRAVING: 20 letters and spaces max. Engraving is\ndone on the timber underneath the lacquer. Please specify if it is\nfor a left or right hander.\n \t* TIMBER BOX LASER ENGRAVING: 50 letters and spaces max (logo,\nsymbols or line drawings are OK).\n \t* _We will contact you to confirm your personalisation prior to it\nbeing complete._\n\nIS IT A GIFT? WE CAN WRAP YOUR PEN AND POST IT DIRECTLY ON YOUR\nBEHALF. Add the name, address of the receiver in the text box, along\nwith your personal message. We will gift wrap and send on your\nbehalf. The package will include your name and a message but will not\ninclude an invoice.\n\n_We are handcrafted Australian timber pen specialists. We would be\npleased to design and turn you a bespoke timber pen. You can even\nsupply your own wood that holds precious memories._\n\nTHE BOSS FOUNTAIN PEN IS A HIGH QUALITY GIFT FOR: Pen collectors,\nentrepreneurs, graduation gifts, birthdays, 5th wedding anniversary\n(wood), Father's Day, I love you, retirement, congratulations,\ncorporate gifts, speaker gifts, or gifts for delegates.\n" <https://www.veridianpenstudio.com.au/product/the-boss-wooden-fountain-pen-cottonwood-timber>   .
