_:n998d480c271f43a3bb86769cc4491f6cxb0 <http://schema.org/description> "### **Job Introduction**\n\nThe BBC is seeking a skilled **Stakeholder Engagement Specialist** to join our Property Project Management team. In this role, you'll lead stakeholder engagement activities across multiple facilities management, property, and construction projects within our extensive UK property estate. Your expertise will be crucial in ensuring effective communication, managing stakeholder expectations, and facilitating smooth project progression through expert stakeholder management.\n\n### **Main Responsibilities**\n\nAs our **Stakeholder Engagement Specialist**, you'll develop and implement comprehensive engagement plans, creating stakeholder maps and influence networks to guide our strategies. You'll design and execute engagement initiatives to keep all parties informed about project progress, changes, and impacts. Facilitating meetings, workshops, and focus groups will be a key part of your role, as will preparing and delivering clear, concise presentations to various stakeholder groups.\n\nActing as the primary liaison between the project team and stakeholders, you&rsquo;ll play a key role in managing expectations, resolving conflicts, and maintaining project documentation. Your strategic input will be valuable in integrating stakeholder engagement into overall project plans and identifying potential risks.\n\n### **Are you the right candidate?**\n\nThe ideal candidate will have strong interpersonal and communication skills, with demonstrable experience working on property projects. Your background should include stakeholder management, preferably in facilities management, property, or construction sectors. Proficiency in stakeholder mapping and analysis techniques is essential, as is familiarity with the UK property market, facilities management practices, and construction processes. Experience with Adobe InDesign and Photoshop is also required.\n\n**Desirable Qualifications**\n\nWe'd be particularly interested in candidates with experience in stakeholder engagement and communications roles, knowledge of project management methodologies (e.g., PRINCE2, APM), and familiarity with digital communication tools used in large organisations. An understanding of sustainability initiatives in property and construction contexts would be a plus.\n\n**What We Offer**\n\nJoin us and you'll have the opportunity to work on diverse projects within the BBC's complex UK property estate. You'll be part of a collaborative team environment and play a crucial role in shaping the future of the BBC's facilities.\n\nIf you're passionate about stakeholder engagement and ready to contribute to the transformation of the BBC estate, we want to hear from you. Apply now and help us build the future of the BBC's facilities.\n\n### **Package Description**\n\nBand:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;C\n\nContract type: &nbsp;Permanent\n\nJob title &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;In-house title is Assistant Project Manager\n\nLocation: &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Office base can be any of the main Hubs. &nbsp;This is a hybrid role and the successful candidate will balance office working with home working\n\nSalary:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &pound;28,000 - &pound;33,000pa (plus London Weighting &pound;5,319pa as London based), **depending on relevant skills, knowledge and experience**. The expected salary range for this role reflects internal benchmarking and external market insights.\n\nWe&rsquo;re happy to discuss flexible working. Please indicate your choice under the flexible working question in the application. There is no obligation to raise this at the application stage but if you wish to do so, you are welcome to. Flexible working will be part of the discussion at offer stage.\n\n- **Excellent career progression** &ndash; the BBC offers great opportunities for employees to seek new challenges and work in different areas of the organisation.\n- **Unrivalled training and development opportunities** &ndash; our in-house Academy hosts a wide range of internal and external courses and certification.\n- **Benefits**- We offer a negotiable salary package, a flexible 35-hour working week for work-life balance and 25 days annual leave with the option to buy an extra 5 days, a defined pension scheme and discounted dental, health care and gym. You can find out more about working at the BBC by selecting this link to our&nbsp;[candidate pack](https://www.bbc.co.uk/academy/courses/this-is-your-bbc/#/).\n\nIf you need to discuss adjustments or access requirements for the interview process please contact the reasonable.adjustments@bbc.co.uk. &nbsp;For any general queries, please contact: bbchr@bbc.co.uk.\n\n**About the BBC**\n\nThe BBC is committed to redeploying employees seeking suitable alternative employment within the BBC for different reasons and they will be given priority consideration ahead of other applicants. Priority consideration means for those employees seeking redeployment their application will be considered alongside anyone else at risk of redundancy, prior to any individuals being considered who are not at risk.\n\nWe don&rsquo;t focus simply on what we do &ndash; we also care how we do it. Our values and the way we behave are important to us. Please make sure you&rsquo;ve read about our values and behaviours [here](https://performancemanager.successfactors.eu/S001190811T2/Our_BBC_Values.pdf).\n\nDiversity matters at the BBC. We have a working environment where we value and respect every individual's unique contribution, enabling all of our employees to thrive and achieve their full potential.\n\nWe want to attract the broadest range of talented people to be part of the BBC &ndash; whether that&rsquo;s to contribute to our programming or our wide range of non-production roles. The more diverse our workforce, the better able we are to respond to and reflect our audiences in all their diversity.\n\nWe are committed to equality of opportunity and welcome applications from individuals, regardless of age, gender, ethnicity, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, socio-economic background, religion and/or belief. We will consider flexible working requests for all roles, unless operational requirements prevent otherwise.\n\nTo find out more about Diversity and Inclusion at the BBC, please click&nbsp;[here](https://www.bbc.co.uk/diversity/).\n\n#LI-DNI" <https://jobboardsearch.com/django-jobs+jobs-in-china>   .
_:n333e3031c7d14957b3d45e298fca5c0axb0 <http://schema.org/description> "### **Package Description**\n\n**Job Reference:** 18842\n\n**Band:** B\n\n**Salary:**&nbsp;&pound;24,300 - &pound;34,300&nbsp; depending on relevant skills, knowledge and experience. The expected salary range for this role reflects internal benchmarking and external market insights.\n\n**Contract type:**&nbsp; Attachment/fixed term contract to end by 31st March 2025\n\n**Location:**&nbsp; Broadcasting House, London\n\nWe&rsquo;re happy to discuss flexible working. Please indicate your choice under the flexible working question in the application. There is no obligation to raise this at the application stage but if you wish to do so, you are welcome to. Flexible working will be part of the discussion at offer stage.\n\n- **Excellent career progression**&ndash; the BBC offers great opportunities for employees to seek new challenges and work in different areas of the organisation.\n- **Unrivalled training and development opportunities** &ndash; our in-house Academy hosts a wide range of internal and external courses and certification.\n- **Benefits** - We offer a negotiable salary package, a flexible 35-hour working week for work-life balance and 25 days annual leave with the option to buy an extra 5 days, a defined pension scheme and discounted dental, health care and gym. You can find out more about working at the BBC by selecting this link to our [candidate pack](https://www.bbc.co.uk/academy/courses/this-is-your-bbc/#/).\n\nIf you need to discuss adjustments or access requirements for the interview process please contact **[reasonable.adjustments@bbc.co.uk](mailto:reasonable.adjustments@bbc.co.uk &quot;mailto:reasonable.adjustments@bbc.co.uk&quot;).**&nbsp;For any general queries, please contact: **[bbchr@bbc.co.uk](mailto:bbchr@bbc.co.uk &quot;mailto:bbchr@bbc.co.uk&quot;)**.\n\n### **Job Introduction**\n\nThe mission of the BBC Concert Orchestra is to bring inspiring musical experiences to everyone, everywhere, with the ensemble&rsquo;s versatility as the key. For BBC Radio 3 the orchestra explores a wide selection of music, ranging from classical to contemporary. It has performed on many soundtracks, including Blue Planet, Serengeti and Wild Isles for BBC One, as well as recording new music for BBC Sounds&rsquo; Music &amp; Meditation podcast and George the Poet&rsquo;s award-winning, Have You Heard George&rsquo;s Podcast? In 2022, it recorded Isobel Waller-Bridge's score for Charlie Mackesy&rsquo;s Oscar winning animated film, The Boy, The Mole, The Fox and The Horse. It performs in BBC Radio 2&rsquo;s Piano Room Month for BBC iPlayer and BBC Sounds, which featured over 20 collaborations with pop artists in 2023, including Stormzy and P!nk.\n\nThe orchestra appears annually at the BBC Proms and regularly at London's Southbank Centre, Nottingham Royal Concert Hall and venues across the UK. The BBC Concert Orchestra takes a leading role in Create Yarmouth, a three-year residency with Orchestras Live, which aims to engage and inspire young people and adults in the Great Yarmouth area, and it has recently embarked on an exciting partnership with the Universities for Nottingham.\n\nThe BBC CO offers enjoyable and innovative education and community activities and, in addition to Create Yarmouth, is also involved in BBC Ten Pieces, the BBC Young Composer competition, and the BBC Open Music programme.\n\nExpected to help research, produce and deliver/publish content by contributing technical, editorial and administrative support to production teams. Expected to help research, produce and deliver/publish content by contributing technical, editorial and administrative support to production teams.\n\n### **Main Responsibilities**\n\nThe Orchestra Content Assistant plays a vital role within the BBC Concert Orchestra, providing support across the operational requirements. This includes administrative and music library support. It is an exciting opportunity to gain a broad experience of working in Live Music and orchestras.\n\nYou will provide a comprehensive administrative service across all projects (including admin support finance tasks, hospitality, travel arrangements, dealing with routine internal and external enquiries). You will assist the orchestra team with administration including auditions, processing payments for players and supporting the on-road operation for players and staff. We may also require you to support our music librarian in music preparation and disposal. You will often be the anchor for a constantly travelling orchestra team.\n\n### **Are you the right candidate?**\n\nYou will ideally have a good awareness of orchestral music and a creative cultural environment. &nbsp;You will be pro-active and have the ability to manage a busy workload across all areas of the Concert Orchestra administration team - you will be prepared to be flexible in support of the business needs of the unit.\n\nYou will need the ability to read music and have an understanding of the structure of orchestras. You will have excellent communication skills in dealing with people at all levels, internal and external contacts, the members of the public and colleagues within the BBC Concert Orchestra. You will be proficient at data entry along with excellent attention to detail.\n\n**We will look to hold interviews in the week of the 21st October 2024 in London.**\n\n**This is for a fixed term role where we&rsquo;d like you to start as soon as possible as this contract must finish by the 31st March 2025.**\n\n### **About the BBC**\n\nThe BBC is committed to redeploying employees seeking suitable alternative employment within the BBC for different reasons and they will be given priority consideration ahead of other applicants. Priority consideration means for those employees seeking redeployment their application will be considered alongside anyone else at risk of redundancy, prior to any individuals being considered who are not at risk.\n\nWe don&rsquo;t focus simply on what we do &ndash; we also care how we do it. Our values and the way we behave are important to us. Please make sure you&rsquo;ve read about our values and behaviours&nbsp;[here](https://performancemanager.successfactors.eu/S001190811T2/Our_BBC_Values.pdf).\n\nDiversity matters at the BBC. We have a working environment where we value and respect every individual's unique contribution, enabling all of our employees to thrive and achieve their full potential.\n\nWe want to attract the broadest range of talented people to be part of the BBC &ndash; whether that&rsquo;s to contribute to our programming or our wide range of non-production roles. The more diverse our workforce, the better able we are to respond to and reflect our audiences in all their diversity.\n\nWe are committed to equality of opportunity and welcome applications from individuals, regardless of age, gender, ethnicity, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, socio-economic background, religion and/or belief. We will consider flexible working requests for all roles, unless operational requirements prevent otherwise.\n\nTo find out more about Diversity and Inclusion at the BBC, please click&nbsp;[here](https://www.bbc.co.uk/diversity/)." <https://jobboardsearch.com/django-jobs+jobs-in-china>   .
_:n6b05ea26fec3424e8928de52b2a6df98xb0 <http://schema.org/description> "### **Package Description**\n\n**Job Reference**: 18241\n\n**Band**: D\n\n**Contract type**: Continuing\n\n**Location:** Media City - Salford, (This is a hybrid role and the successful candidate will balance office with home working)\n\n**Salary**: &pound;42,000 - &pound;52,000 depending on relevant skills, knowledge and experience. The expected salary range for this role reflects internal benchmarking and external market insights.\n\nWe&rsquo;re happy to discuss flexible working. Please indicate your choice under the flexible working question in the application. There is no obligation to raise this at the application stage but if you wish to do so, you are welcome to. Flexible working will be part of the discussion at offer stage.\n\n**Excellent career progression**&ndash; the BBC offers great opportunities for employees to seek new challenges and work in different areas of the organisation.\n\n**Unrivalled training and development opportunities**&ndash; our in-house Academy hosts a wide range of internal and external courses and certification.\n\n**Benefits**- We offer a negotiable salary package, a flexible 35-hour working week for work-life balance and 25 days annual leave with the option to buy an extra 5 days, a defined pension scheme and discounted dental, health care and gym. You can find out more about working at the BBC by selecting this link to our [candidate pack](https://www.bbc.co.uk/academy/courses/this-is-your-bbc/#/).\n\nIf you need to discuss adjustments or access requirements for the interview process please contact the reasonable.adjustments@bbc.co.uk &nbsp; For any general queries, please contact: bbchr@bbc.co.uk.\n\n### **Job Introduction**\n\nBBC Creative is the BBC&rsquo;s in-house Creative agency. &nbsp;Our purpose is to make as many people as possible love and value the BBC, by creating campaigns that will leave a positive mark on popular culture! We are now looking for a talented Production Manager to join our Production team.\n\nYou would join a team of creatively minded producers responsible for delivering the promotional campaigns and branding for the BBC, its content and services across all platforms &ndash; TV, digital, social, OOH etc.\n\nOur work varies hugely - from the Olympic Games , Traitors, Hey Duggee and Galdiators working across all the brands and genres &ndash; from BBC One to Radio 1, iPlayer to Cbeebies, Drama to Live events.\n\nIf you like a challenge, then this is the place for you!\n\n### **Main Responsibilities**\n\n- You will be responsible for scheduling, budgeting and managing the production(s) in line with divisional requirements, as well as identifying and sourcing appropriate resource and location requirements for the production(s) at the earliest possible stage.\n- Ensure compliance with BBC policies, guidelines, legislative and regulatory requirements, in order to minimise the BBCs exposure to risk and to deliver value for money through effective and efficient management of people and resources.\n- You will also be responsible for preparing, managing and monitoring production budgets, and for forecasting and reporting progress in line with best practice.\n- You&rsquo;ll help brands thrive and develop in the digital space across multiple platforms\n- Produce hi-end multiplatform campaigns devised by BBC Creative, and ensure that that all output is high quality and is delivered on time and to budget.\n- Create detailed cost estimates, timing plans, specification documents and communicating them to the team.\n\n\n### **Are you the right candidate?**\n\n- Experience of working within the BBC editorial guidelines , legal, safeguarding, music copyright and all the relevant paperwork including Risk Assessments.\n- Leadership &ndash; Managing a campaign team &nbsp;including production staff, creatives, designers, editors and external production partners\n- Experience of producing budgets, schedules &nbsp;scoping scripts and managing post production workflows\n- Ability to &nbsp;produce short-form multi-platform integrated campaigns (in an advertising or similar)\n- Experience of managing and &nbsp;collaborating with stakeholders\n\n\n### **About the BBC**\n\nThe BBC is committed to redeploying employees seeking suitable alternative employment within the BBC for different reasons and they will be given priority consideration ahead of other applicants. Priority consideration means for those employees seeking redeployment their application will be considered alongside anyone else at risk of redundancy, prior to any individuals being considered who are not at risk.\n\nWe don&rsquo;t focus simply on what we do &ndash; we also care how we do it. Our values and the way we behave are important to us. Please make sure you&rsquo;ve read about our values and behaviours here.\n\nDiversity matters at the BBC. We have a working environment where we value and respect every individual's unique contribution, enabling all of our employees to thrive and achieve their full potential.\n\nWe want to attract the broadest range of talented people to be part of the BBC &ndash; whether that&rsquo;s to contribute to our programming or our wide range of non-production roles. The more diverse our workforce, the better able we are to respond to and reflect our audiences in all their diversity.\n\nWe are committed to equality of opportunity and welcome applications from individuals, regardless of age, gender, ethnicity, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, socio-economic background, religion and/or belief. We will consider flexible working requests for all roles, unless operational requirements prevent otherwise.\n\nTo find out more about Diversity and Inclusion at the BBC, please click here." <https://jobboardsearch.com/django-jobs+jobs-in-china>   .
