_:nea112df4ccff40c89702d9890624dc35xb0 <http://schema.org/articleBody> "<p>Facebook reportedly withheld a significant amount of information about the ways people use its platform from researchers examining the spread of misinformation on the social network. It blames a technical error that went unnoticed for the two years the program was active.</p><p><em>The New York Times </em><a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/live/2020/2020-election-misinformation-distortions\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"(Opens in a new tab)\">reports</a> that researchers expected to receive&mdash;and were told they had been provided&mdash;all of the data Facebook had relating to user interaction in the US. But they were only given access to information related to half of the social network's American users.</p><p>The report says Facebook only provided information about US users \"who engaged with political pages enough to make their political leanings clear.\" But the company also claimed that data about its users outside the US \"did not appear to be inaccurate,\" as the <em>Times</em> puts it.</p><p>Facebook reportedly said in an email that it was working to gather the rest of the data, but it wouldn't be ready for several weeks because of the sheer amount of information involved. It also said it \"would like to offer as much support as possible\" to affected researchers.</p><div class=\"roundup-offers my-4 border-x-0 border-b-2 border-red-400 py-8\" id=\"offers-groups\">\n        <div class=\"line-header decorative-horizontal-lines flex before:border-red-400 after:border-red-400\">\n            <div class=\"flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-red-400\">\n                <svg class=\"w-6 h-6 text-white z-1 mr-[0.1rem]\" version=\"1.1\" id=\"Layer_1\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" x=\"0px\" y=\"0px\" viewbox=\"0 0 160.7 148.5\" style=\"enable-background:new 0 0 160.7 148.5;\" xml:space=\"preserve\">\n<path fill=\"currentColor\" d=\"M152.4,89.6l-90.6,56.6c-6.9,4.3-16,2.2-20.4-4.7L2.3,79.2c-4.3-6.9-2.2-16,4.7-20.3L97.5,2.3\n\tc4.2-2.6,9.4-3,13.9-1l45,20.2c2.7,1.2,4.4,4,4.4,6.9l-1.4,49.2C159.2,82.5,156.6,87,152.4,89.6z M145.8,32.9l-40.5-18.2L14.8,71.3\n\tL54,133.8l90.6-56.6L145.8,32.9z M115.8,51.7c-2.2-3.4-1.1-8,2.3-10.2c3.5-2.2,8-1.1,10.2,2.3c2.2,3.4,1.1,8-2.3,10.2\n\tC122.5,56.2,118,55.1,115.8,51.7z\"></path>\n</svg>            </div>\n        </div>\n                    <h3 class=\"font-stretch-ultra-condensed my-6 flex justify-center font-semibold\">The Best Amazon Prime Day Deals Right Now</h3>\n                <ul style=\"list-style-type: none; padding-left: 0;\">\n                            <li>\n                    <a href=\"https://cc.pcmag.com/v1/otc/01r1WRIAJykbQgN4oGQ8FSi?merchant=05kie42h3YvHwjr4G1w80Qq&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.amazon.com%2Fdp%2FB0D1XD1ZV3&amp;template=article-page&amp;module=offers-group&amp;element=offer-group&amp;item=Apple+AirPods+Pro+2+ANC+Earbuds+With+USB-C+Charging+Case&amp;position=1&amp;element_label=Apple+AirPods+Pro+2+ANC+Earbuds+With+USB-C+Charging+Case&amp;u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.pcmag.com%2Fnews%2Ffacebook-didnt-give-researchers-the-data-it-promised&amp;object_type=offer&amp;object_uuid=072KyLrpKMRilHLrTfH2Jn2&amp;product_uuid=05XR1ryVbywEqNr8FPjeE3K\" data-commerce=\"1\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"(Opens in a new tab)\" rel=\"sponsored\" data-parent-group=\"affiliate-link\" class=\"roundup-offer-link font-stretch-condensed\" style=\"\" offer-uuid=\"072KyLrpKMRilHLrTfH2Jn2\" data-aps-asin=\"B0D1XD1ZV3\" data-aps-asc-tag=\"p00935-20\" data-aps-asc-subtag=\"072KyLrpKMRilHLrTfH2Jn2\" x-track-ga-click=\"1\" data-element=\"offer-group\" data-action=\"Apple AirPods Pro 2 ANC Earbuds With USB-C Charging Case\" data-item=\"Apple AirPods Pro 2 ANC Earbuds With USB-C Charging Case\" data-position=\"1\" data-module=\"offers-group\">\n    Apple AirPods Pro 2 ANC Earbuds With USB-C Charging Case\n</a>\n                                            for\n       